  "limitations": [
    "Reference PS custody is explicitly unqualified trusted same-process JavaScript/BigInt; provider adapters are injected and can undermine confidentiality. No sandbox, constant-time, non-exportable-key or zeroization claim.",
    "Monotonic timers reject late results but cannot preempt blocked JavaScript or synchronous filesystem work; no whole-operation hard resource/latency guarantee or production throughput qualification.",
    "Private path checks and local PID locks require controlled local directories/parents; no openat-relative or malicious-same-user/privileged race defense, distributed fencing or network-filesystem qualification.",
    "Authentic selected records can be old. Operator checkpoint/fencing acknowledgement records an assertion, not proof of global freshness. Receipts are snapshots, not reservations.",
